# What reaches the BUILD MACHINE — no longer what gets published.
#
# Since 2026-08-07 the deploy publishes dist-site/, assembled by site/build_site.js from
# an allowlist, so this file no longer decides what visitors can reach. It only trims the
# upload. That change was made because Cloudflare Pages honours no ignore file at all:
# relying on this one to hold back test/, Blueprint/, Manuals/ and the dev harness pages
# stops working the moment the host changes, and publishing the repo root was always the
# fragile choice.
#
# It still matters for one thing: a build script that vercel.json runs must not be
# excluded here, or the deploy fails with a bare exit 1 (Alpha 1.10.0). test/run_portable.js
# checks exactly that.
node_modules
test
Diagnostic
inbox
mcps
# NOT the whole of tools/: vercel.json's buildCommand runs site/make_download.js, which
# shells out to tools/make_portable.js to build the offline download. Excluding the
# directory made the deploy fail with exit 1 (Alpha 1.10.0). Ignore-file semantics do not
# let you re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so the dev-only tools are listed
# individually instead. A new tool added here ships to the deploy unless you add it — that
# fails OPEN (a slightly larger bundle) rather than breaking the build.
tools/gen_board_data.js
tools/gen_manual_reference.js
tools/hook_repack_manuals.js
tools/make_portable.cmd
tools/pack_manuals.js
tools/stamp_manual_revision.js
Blueprint
terminals
Manuals
# dev harness pages
test_pwr.html
test_bwr.html
test_rbmk.html
# The usage-data receiver is a separate Cloudflare Worker with its own deploy
# (worker/README.md). It is not part of the site and must not be published with it —
# it would serve wrangler.toml, including the bucket and dataset names, as static files.
worker
